TITLE:: SampleEditor
summary:: a window on one sound file: trim, gain, DC, fades, numbers, bpm grid, slicer, save into SuperDirt banks
categories:: Libraries>SampleEditor
related:: Classes/SampleEditorHost, Classes/SampleEditorDirtHost, Classes/SampleEdit, Classes/SampleCutter

DESCRIPTION::
The waveform, one lane per channel, with the trim markers on the top strip and
the fade handles on the bottom; boxes for the same in milliseconds; a gain knob
with normalize to a ceiling; remove DC; a table of numbers for the file
as it is and for what the save would write; the analysis (bpm and its grid,
key, tags); the slicer and what it keeps; play and stop; open, reset, revert,
save, save as, to bank.

code::
SampleEditor("~/somewhere/kick.wav");                           // plays to the hardware outputs
SampleEditor("~/somewhere/kick.wav", SampleEditorDirtHost(~dirt));   // through SuperDirt's orbits
SampleEditor.defaultHost = SampleEditorDirtHost(~dirt);         // for every editor from now on
SampleEditor.sample(\bd, 3);                                    // bd:3 of the host's library
::

What the editor knows of the world is its emphasis::host::. The plain
link::Classes/SampleEditorHost:: plays to the server's hardware outputs and
only writes files. link::Classes/SampleEditorDirtHost:: plays through a
SuperDirt's orbits and knows its library: a file it holds opens as
code::bd:3::, a save is read back into the same Buffer so Tidal plays it at
once, a bank written is loaded. SuperDirtGUI makes one that also keeps the
files' tags, and sets it as link::#*defaultHost:: while it runs.

A sound file dropped from the Finder on the window opens in an editor - in this
window's place when nothing here was changed yet, else beside it
(link::#-openFiles::); strong::open...:: does the same through the Finder's
dialog. strong::to bank...:: writes the trim into a bank's folder and hands it
to the host (link::#-addToBank::), so a file is cut into parts one selection at
a time.

Nothing is written until save. The file is read into the language
(link::Classes/SampleEdit::), every setting sits on top of it, and the
preview is the host's Buffer for the file (or one read for it) through a small
synth into the output picked in the window - with a SuperDirt host, at the head
of the orbit's group into its dry bus, so its effects and fader apply - with
the trim, the gain, the fades and the DC applied on the way. The host wakes the
output first: SuperDirt's monitor sleeps after four seconds of silence.

strong::save:: writes over the file, in its own header and sample format, and
keeps the original beside it as code::.bak:: the first time only; then the host
hears of it (link::Classes/SampleEditorHost#-fileChanged::): a SuperDirt host
reads the new file into the same Buffer, so Tidal plays it at once under the
same name and number. strong::revert:: copies the code::.bak:: back.
strong::save as...:: writes a new file; into the bank's own folder and it is
appended to the bank as its last index. An integer format is clipped just under
full scale on the way out; a float file keeps its overs.

The numbers are exact, in the language: peak, rms and crest from one pass
over the samples, the DC offset of each channel, integrated loudness and the
loudest 400 ms window K-weighted and gated as ITU-R BS.1770 says - a stretch
shorter than a block is read as one block and says code::(short)::. Loudness
sums channels as the spec does: identical left and right read 3 dB above mono.

Under the header is what the analysis says about the file
(link::Classes/SampleFeatures::, and the host's tag store when it has one): the
bpm, sure, unsure or by hand; where a beat falls; the key, or the note of a
one-shot; the tags; and the numbers they came from. The window analyses the
whole file when it opens, in the background (link::#-analyse::). With a bpm the
beat grid is drawn over the wave: bars numbered in the accent colour, beats,
and the slicer's division, each when there is room. ÷2 and ×2 halve and double
it, to 1st hit puts a beat on the first attack (link::#-snapGridToFirstHit::),
alt + drag on the wave slides it. With a store, a bpm, key or tags set here are
the file's from then on, by hand; without one they last as long as the window.

The slicer (link::Classes/SampleCutter::) cuts the trim on the grid at a division,
or on the attacks at a sensitivity, and shows the cuts on the wave as they move
- in attacks mode with the onset curve they come from. shift + click on the
wave adds a cut, or takes away the one under the pointer. The keep row drops
slices too quiet, too short or too long from the export, cmd + click puts one in
or out by hand. export slices... (link::#-exportSlicesDialog::) asks where, in
the Finder's folder dialog, and under what name, then writes every kept slice to
a new folder of that name, each file named after it with the slice's index from
0, and hands the folder to the host; the file itself is not written to.

Keys, when the window has focus: space plays and stops, code::0:: shows the
whole file, code::-:: and code::=:: zoom, code::f:: zooms to the trim, code::g::
shows and hides the grid, left and right slide, cmd-s saves. In the waveform:
cmd + two fingers up and down zooms at the pointer, two fingers on their own
slide, a double click shows the whole file, alt + double click the trim. On Windows and Linux it is ctrl where
it says cmd (link::#*isShortcut::), and the wheel where it says two fingers.

One editor per file: opening a file that is already open fronts its
window. The list is link::#*all::.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
An editor on a file, open.
ARGUMENT:: path
the file.
ARGUMENT:: host
a link::Classes/SampleEditorHost:: or anything answering its messages; nil for link::#*defaultHost::.
ARGUMENT:: output
the index of the host's output the preview plays into: an orbit with a SuperDirt host.
ARGUMENT:: bounds
where the window goes; nil for link::#*windowBounds::.
RETURNS:: the SampleEditor - the one already open on that file if there is one.

METHOD:: sample
An editor on the file a host's library holds as name:index.
ARGUMENT:: name
the bank.
ARGUMENT:: index
the sample in it.
ARGUMENT:: host
nil for link::#*defaultHost::.
ARGUMENT:: output
as for link::#*new::.

METHOD:: defaultHost
The host an editor gets when given none: the one set, else a plain
link::Classes/SampleEditorHost:: on code::Server.default::. SuperDirtGUI sets
its own here and takes it away when freed.

METHOD:: makeKnob
A knob dragged up and down, whose double click sets it back to its default
through its action.
ARGUMENT:: size
pixels.
ARGUMENT:: centered
drawn from the middle.
ARGUMENT:: default
a unit value, or a function answering one; nil for no reset.

METHOD:: colBg
METHOD:: colPanel
METHOD:: colText
METHOD:: colDim
METHOD:: colAccent
METHOD:: colOn
METHOD:: colWarn
METHOD:: colWave
METHOD:: colWaveDim
METHOD:: colWaveBg
METHOD:: colHandle
METHOD:: colPlay
The window's colours.

METHOD:: droppedPaths
The existing files and folders in what a drag from outside brings: one path
as a String, several as an Array; a code::file://:: prefix is taken off.
ARGUMENT:: data
code::View.currentDrag::.
RETURNS:: an link::Classes/Array:: of paths.

METHOD:: isSoundFile
Whether a path is a file with a sound file's extension (wav, aiff, flac, ogg, mp3, caf ...).
ARGUMENT:: path
the path.

METHOD:: acceptDrops
Make a view take drops from the Finder.
ARGUMENT:: view
the view.
ARGUMENT:: action
called with the dropped paths (link::#*droppedPaths::).
ARGUMENT:: test
code::{ |paths| }:: answering whether to take them; nil takes any drop holding a sound file.

METHOD:: fileChooser
A function code::{ |ok| }:: used in place of the Finder's open dialog, answering
paths through code::ok::; nil for the dialog. Checks set it.

METHOD:: bankParent
METHOD:: lastBank
Where link::#-addToBank:: last wrote (the folder the bank folder is in) and
the bank's name: the next to bank... window starts there.

METHOD:: all
The open editors.

METHOD:: folderChooser
A function code::{ |start, ok| }:: used in place of the Finder's folder dialog,
answering a folder through code::ok::; nil for the dialog. Checks set it.

METHOD:: chooseFolder
The Finder's folder dialog, or link::#*folderChooser::.
ARGUMENT:: start
the folder it opens at.
ARGUMENT:: ok
called with the folder picked, without a trailing slash, on AppClock; not called on cancel.

METHOD:: windowBounds
Where the last closed editor was; the next one opens there.

METHOD:: isShortcut
Whether a key's modifiers are the shortcut modifier: cmd on macOS, ctrl on
Windows and Linux - which is how QtCollider reports the key there.
ARGUMENT:: mod
the modifiers a keyDownAction is given.

METHOD:: saveKeyName
code::"cmd-s":: on macOS, code::"ctrl-s":: elsewhere: what the hints call the
save shortcut.

METHOD:: previewDef
METHOD:: previewDefName
The preview SynthDef for a sample with that many channels into that many, and
its name, code::sampleeditor_preview_<src>_<out>::.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: edit
The link::Classes/SampleEdit:: behind the window.

METHOD:: host
The link::Classes/SampleEditorHost:: it was made with.

METHOD:: server
The host's server.

METHOD:: outputIndex
The output the preview plays into; the menu in the window sets it.

METHOD:: play
METHOD:: stop
METHOD:: isPlaying
The preview. It frees itself at the end of the trim.

METHOD:: refresh
Everything on screen from the model.

METHOD:: analyse
The features of the whole file again, in a Routine on AppClock; the grid
takes the file's bpm as the host's store knows it, or the analysis's.
ARGUMENT:: force
true analyses the file in the store again too.

METHOD:: info
What the store's code::infoOf:: says about the file, or nil without a store.

METHOD:: store
The host's tag store (SuperDirtGUI's code::SDGSampleTags::), or nil.

METHOD:: setBpm
The grid's bpm, kept for the file by hand; nil takes the grid away.
ARGUMENT:: bpm
a number, or nil.

METHOD:: setKey
ARGUMENT:: str
a key, code::"Am"::, code::"F#"::, code::"C3"::; empty for the analysis's.

METHOD:: setTags
ARGUMENT:: words
the file's tags, all of them.

METHOD:: snapGridToFirstHit
A beat of the grid on the first attack of the file, to the sample
(link::Classes/SampleEdit#-refineOnset::).

METHOD:: slicing
Whether the slicer is on, as its check box.

METHOD:: slicer
The link::Classes/SampleCutter:: while the slicer is on, else nil.

METHOD:: exportSlices
Every slice into a folder, then a bank, with a hint saying how to play it.
ARGUMENT:: folder
the new folder's path; nil for link::Classes/SampleCutter#-defaultFolder::, beside the file.
RETURNS:: what link::Classes/SampleCutter#-export:: answers, or nil.

METHOD:: exportSlicesDialog
The export slices... button: link::#*chooseFolder:: at
link::Classes/SampleCutter#*exportStart::, then a window asking for the folder's
name, showing the files it will write; return or export writes them through
link::#-exportSlices::, escape cancels.

METHOD:: exportDialog
While that window is open: code::(window:, folder:, export:, preview:)::, where
code::folder:: and code::preview:: are functions answering the place and the
text shown, and code::export.(name):: exports under a name as the button does.

METHOD:: openFiles
Open files, one editor each; the first takes this window's place when nothing
here was changed (no trim, gain, DC, fades, cuts by hand) and it is not playing.
What a drop on the window does. Folders and other files are left out.
ARGUMENT:: paths
the files.
RETURNS:: the editors opened.

METHOD:: openDialog
The open... button: the Finder's dialog (or link::#*fileChooser::), several
files allowed, then link::#-openFiles::.

METHOD:: addToBank
The trim into a bank's folder through link::Classes/SampleEdit#-addToBank::,
loaded at once; remembers link::#*bankParent:: and link::#*lastBank::.
ARGUMENT:: folder
the bank's folder; made when new.
RETURNS:: code::(path:, bank:, index:)::, or nil.

METHOD:: addToBankDialog
The to bank... button: a window asking for the bank's name, at
link::#*bankParent:: (Dirt-Samples the first time), showing the file it will
write and the code::s "bank:n":: it will play as; return or add writes through
link::#-addToBank::, escape cancels, change... picks another place - a bank's
own folder picks that bank.

METHOD:: bankDialog
While that window is open: code::(window:, folder:, add:, preview:, pick:)::;
code::add.(name):: adds under a name as the button does, code::pick.(path)::
is what change... does with the folder picked.

METHOD:: window
METHOD:: isOpen
METHOD:: front
METHOD:: close
The window's state. Closing stops the preview, frees a buffer read for a file
outside the library, and forgets the editor.
